<title>UK: Lowndes Lambert H1 pretax profit dips.</title>
<headline>Lowndes Lambert H1 pretax profit dips.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		 5.4		   vs   6.9</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  2.9		   vs   2.9</p>
<p> Pretax			5.0		   vs   6.0</p>
<p> Turnover		   40.4		   vs  36.4</p>
<p> Administrative Expenses  37.6		 vs   33.7</p>
<p> Interest receivable	 1.5		 vs    1.9</p>
<p> Tax			     1.6		 vs    1.8</p>
<p> Net taxed		     3.4		 vs    4.2</p>
<p> Attributable		  3.3		 vs    4.1</p>
<p> Pay date		   February 3, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  January 14, 1997</p>
<p> Ex-div date		January 6, 1997</p>
<p>Note: Insurance firm Lowndes Lambert said phasing of profit in its recent acquisitions and investments in staff and systems resulted in lower profits.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44-171-542 7717</p>
</text>
